  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Players in turn play one card to capture: a table card of the same rank, or a set of table cards whose total equals the played card, or three of a rank from hand to capture the fourth from the table. Captured cards form a trick placed face down. If unable to capture (e.g. after a sauterelle sweep), the player trails all hand cards face up to the tableau. When all hands are empty, the dealer gives 3 more cards each from the talon. When the talon is exhausted, the first to empty their hand by taking a trick wins the deal (papillon) and sweeps the pool.',
    Player: 'Players in turn play one card to capture: a table card of the same rank, or a set of table cards whose total equals the played card, or three of a rank from hand to capture the fourth from the table. Captured cards form a trick placed face down. If unable to capture (e.g. after a sauterelle sweep), the player trails all hand cards face up to the tableau. When all hands are empty, the dealer gives 3 more cards each from the talon. When the talon is exhausted, the first to empty their hand by taking a trick wins the deal (papillon) and sweeps the pool.',
    objective: 'Score points by capturing cards and clearing the table; be the first to empty your hand after the talon is exhausted (papillon) to sweep the pool.',
    gameplay: 'Players in turn play one card to capture: a table card of the same rank, or a set of table cards whose total equals the played card, or three of a rank from hand to capture the fourth from the table. Captured cards form a trick placed face down. If unable to capture (e.g. after a sauterelle sweep), the player trails all hand cards face up to the tableau. When all hands are empty, the dealer gives 3 more cards each from the talon. When the talon is exhausted, the first to empty their hand by taking a trick wins the deal (papillon) and sweeps the pool.',
    keyRules: [
      'Capture by same rank, by sum (played card equals total of table cards), or three-of-a-rank to take the fourth from table.',
      'If you cannot capture, you must trail (play all hand cards face up to the tableau).',
      'Sauterelle: sweeping all table cards forces the next player to trail.',
      'Winner of the deal is first to empty hand by taking a trick after talon is exhausted; tie-break: dealer, second hand, first hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
