    turnFlow: 'Players in turn play one card to capture: a table card of the same rank, or a set of table cards whose total equals the played card, or three of a rank from hand to capture the fourth from the table. Captured cards form a trick placed face down. If unable to capture (e.g. after a sauterelle sweep), the player trails all hand cards face up to the tableau. When all hands are empty, the dealer gives 3 more cards each from the talon. When the talon is exhausted, the first to empty their hand by taking a trick wins the deal (papillon) and sweeps the pool.',
